# =============================================================================
# Build-context exclusions for the web image.
#
# The repository-root .dockerignore does not apply here: this image is built
# with apps/web as its context, and Docker reads the ignore file belonging to
# the context it is given.
#
# node_modules is the one that actually breaks a build rather than merely
# slowing it. The Dockerfile installs dependencies and then copies the source
# over the top; without this line the host's node_modules - built against the
# host's platform and architecture - would be copied over the freshly installed
# Linux ones, and the build would fail on a native binary that is not for this
# operating system.
# =============================================================================

node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never bake local environment overrides into an image. They routinely point at
# a developer's own machine, and inlined into the bundle they would ship that.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
